      "role": "user",
      "content": "ok got it. so if i'm using 6x6 posts and 2x10 joists, what should i be looking out for regarding structural failure or unexpected stresses that could make the deck unsafe? like are there common mistakes people make with load distribution that lead to sag or collapse?",
      "source": "evaluator"
    },
    {
      "role": "assistant",
      "content": "When using 6x6 posts and 2x10 joists, the biggest pitfalls usually involve connection points and load paths. A common mistake is underestimating the shear forces at the beam-to-post connections, which can lead to racking or sudden failure, not just sag. Another major issue is improper joist spacing, which directly impacts how much load the 2x10s can carry before they deflect too much (sagging). Always ensure your load is distributed evenly across the entire structure, not just concentrated in one spot, which is where the real dangers lurk.",
      "source": "target",
